<b>In 1943, the UPA published a leaflet</b>

240
01:06:59,199 --> 01:07:00,533
<b>calling "What the Ukrainian</b>

241
01:07:00,566 --> 01:07:01,866
<b>insurgent army is fighting</b>

242
01:07:01,866 --> 01:07:02,233
<b>for".</b>

243
01:07:02,433 --> 01:07:04,199
<b>It says the UPA is fighting for an</b>

244
01:07:04,199 --> 01:07:05,433
<b>independent, united</b>

245
01:07:05,466 --> 01:07:07,466
<b>Ukrainian state and against Russian</b>

246
01:07:07,466 --> 01:07:09,433
<b>Bolshevik and German occupiers.</b>

247
01:07:09,533 --> 01:07:10,366
<b>That tells us what the</b>

248
01:07:10,366 --> 01:07:11,833
<b>movement said about itself.</b>

249
01:07:11,900 --> 01:07:13,433
<b>But did they actually keep fighting the</b>

250
01:07:13,433 --> 01:07:15,599
<b>Soviet rule once the Red Army came back?</b>

251
01:07:15,633 --> 01:07:16,466
<b>This is where Soviet</b>

252
01:07:16,466 --> 01:07:18,033
<b>records become much more useful.</b>

253
01:07:18,133 --> 01:07:21,033
<b>In June 1945, the Ukrainian Soviet secret</b>

254
01:07:21,033 --> 01:07:22,500
<b>police sent instructions</b>

255
01:07:22,500 --> 01:07:23,733
<b>to its regional officers</b>

256
01:07:23,733 --> 01:07:25,433
<b>about OUN members getting</b>

257
01:07:25,433 --> 01:07:27,033
<b>inside Soviet institutions.</b>

258
01:07:27,466 --> 01:07:29,233
<b>The document says they were working</b>

259
01:07:29,233 --> 01:07:29,800
<b>inside local</b>

260
01:07:29,800 --> 01:07:32,266
<b>administrations, land agencies, post</b>

261
01:07:32,266 --> 01:07:34,699
<b>and telephone services, military offices</b>

262
01:07:34,733 --> 01:07:36,433
<b>and other Soviet institutions.</b>

263
01:07:36,599 --> 01:07:38,033
<b>They were gathering information about</b>

264
01:07:38,033 --> 01:07:39,433
<b>officials, security</b>

265
01:07:39,433 --> 01:07:41,133
<b>arrangements, prisoners and troop</b>

266
01:07:41,133 --> 01:07:41,766
<b>movements.</b>

267
01:07:42,033 --> 01:07:43,033
<b>And that information</b>

268
01:07:43,033 --> 01:07:44,533
<b>could be used to plan attacks.</b>

269
01:07:45,033 --> 01:07:47,366
<b>The NKVD document actually warns that</b>

270
01:07:47,599 --> 01:07:48,866
<b>Soviet institutions and</b>

271
01:07:48,900 --> 01:07:50,466
<b>enterprises are swamped by</b>

272
01:07:50,466 --> 01:07:51,666
<b>a hostile element.</b>

273
01:07:51,733 --> 01:07:52,599
<b>Those are the people</b>

274
01:07:52,599 --> 01:07:53,933
<b>trying to destroy the movement.</b>

275
01:07:54,099 --> 01:07:56,099
<b>And their own records are saying OUN</b>

276
01:07:56,133 --> 01:07:57,633
<b>members are getting inside Soviet</b>

277
01:07:57,633 --> 01:07:59,066
<b>institutions, collecting</b>

278
01:07:59,066 --> 01:07:59,900
<b>intelligence and</b>

279
01:07:59,900 --> 01:08:01,599
<b>helping armed groups operate.</b>

280
01:08:01,933 --> 01:08:03,833
<b>Soviet records also describe major</b>

281
01:08:03,833 --> 01:08:05,500
<b>operations, arrests,</b>

282
01:08:05,666 --> 01:08:08,033
<b>infiltration and deportations aimed</b>

283
01:08:08,033 --> 01:08:09,466
<b>at destroying the underground and the</b>

284
01:08:09,466 --> 01:08:10,699
<b>people supporting it.</b>

285
01:08:10,866 --> 01:08:14,166
<b>So this really was an organized</b>

286
01:08:14,166 --> 01:08:15,866
<b>resistance, not only something the</b>

287
01:08:15,866 --> 01:08:16,800
<b>movement claimed about</b>

288
01:08:16,800 --> 01:08:17,566
<b>itself.</b>

289
01:08:18,100 --> 01:08:20,600
<b>By the end of the 1940s, the large UPA</b>

290
01:08:20,633 --> 01:08:22,533
<b>formations had mostly disappeared.</b>

291
01:08:22,899 --> 01:08:25,000
<b>But smaller OUN and security service</b>

292
01:08:25,000 --> 01:08:27,566
<b>groups continued into the 1950s.</b>

293
01:08:27,766 --> 01:08:29,566
<b>And the underground also coerced and</b>

294
01:08:29,566 --> 01:08:30,666
<b>killed Ukrainians, it's</b>

295
01:08:30,666 --> 01:08:31,633
<b>suspected of helping the</b>

296
01:08:31,633 --> 01:08:32,333
<b>Soviets.</b>

297
01:08:32,633 --> 01:08:34,933
<b>So no, recognizing that the struggle was</b>

298
01:08:34,933 --> 01:08:36,266
<b>real does not make these</b>

299
01:08:36,266 --> 01:08:37,866
<b>people angels or excuse</b>

300
01:08:37,899 --> 01:08:39,199
<b>everything else they did.</b>

301
01:08:39,533 --> 01:08:40,966
<b>But the struggle was real.</b>

302
01:08:41,166 --> 01:08:42,899
<b>Now let's go back to the textbook.</b>

303
01:08:43,100 --> 01:08:44,733
<b>The part about expelling Poles and</b>

304
01:08:44,733 --> 01:08:45,966
<b>attacking Polish settlements</b>

305
01:08:46,000 --> 01:08:47,199
<b>is supported by the historical</b>

306
01:08:47,199 --> 01:08:47,800
<b>record.</b>

307
01:08:48,066 --> 01:08:49,033
<b>So is the part about</b>

308
01:08:49,066 --> 01:08:50,300
<b>fighting Soviet rule.</b>

309
01:08:50,466 --> 01:08:53,300
<b>Both basic claims check out, but only one</b>

310
01:08:53,300 --> 01:08:54,733
<b>gets described as heroic.</b>

311
01:08:54,933 --> 01:08:56,833
<b>One textbook obviously cannot tell us</b>

312
01:08:56,833 --> 01:08:57,766
<b>what every Ukrainian</b>

313
01:08:57,766 --> 01:08:59,466
<b>thinks, but it does show how</b>

314
01:08:59,466 --> 01:09:01,199
<b>these two things can coexist.</b>

315
01:09:01,533 --> 01:09:03,933
<b>Volnya can be there in the history and at</b>

316
01:09:03,933 --> 01:09:05,033
<b>the same time the</b>

317
01:09:05,033 --> 01:09:06,399
<b>anti-Soviet struggle can</b>

318
01:09:06,399 --> 01:09:07,800
<b>become the part of the UPA's</b>

319
01:09:07,800 --> 01:09:09,500
<b>history that gets commemorated.</b>

320
01:09:09,766 --> 01:09:10,766
<b>That idea was already</b>

321
01:09:10,766 --> 01:09:12,566
<b>developing before the current war.</b>

322
01:09:12,766 --> 01:09:15,033
<b>The 2010 Ukrainian presidential decree</b>

323
01:09:15,199 --> 01:09:17,166
<b>includes OUN and UPA members</b>

324
01:09:17,233 --> 01:09:18,800
<b>among 20th century fighters</b>

325
01:09:18,833 --> 01:09:20,300
<b>for Ukrainian independence.</b>

326
01:09:20,533 --> 01:09:23,866
<b>Then in 2015, after Russia seized Crimea</b>

327
01:09:23,933 --> 01:09:24,800
<b>and the war in Donbas</b>

328
01:09:24,800 --> 01:09:26,433
<b>began, Ukraine passed a</b>

329
01:09:26,433 --> 01:09:28,899
<b>law recognizing OUN and UPA as</b>

330
01:09:28,899 --> 01:09:30,300
<b>organizations which fought</b>

331
01:09:30,300 --> 01:09:32,033
<b>for Ukrainian independence and</b>

332
01:09:32,033 --> 01:09:33,166
<b>made commemoration of that</b>

333
01:09:33,166 --> 01:09:34,766
<b>struggle part of state policy.</b>

334
01:09:35,000 --> 01:09:35,766
<b>And I think the change</b>

335
01:09:35,766 --> 01:09:37,966
<b>after 2014 is pretty obvious.</b>

336
01:09:38,199 --> 01:09:39,399
<b>Resistance to Moscow was</b>

337
01:09:39,399 --> 01:09:40,666
<b>no longer only history.</b>

338
01:09:41,066 --> 01:09:42,833
<b>After Russia's full-scale invasion in</b>

339
01:09:42,833 --> 01:09:45,666
<b>2022, that became even more relevant.</b>

340
01:09:45,966 --> 01:09:48,133
<b>The 2026 decree which gave the current</b>

341
01:09:48,133 --> 01:09:49,300
<b>military unit the name</b>

342
01:09:49,300 --> 01:09:50,966
<b>"Heroes of the UPA" actually</b>

343
01:09:50,966 --> 01:09:52,133
<b>says this directly.</b>

344
01:09:52,500 --> 01:09:54,300
<b>It says the name is meant to restore the</b>

345
01:09:54,300 --> 01:09:55,500
<b>historical traditions of</b>

346
01:09:55,500 --> 01:09:57,199
<b>Ukraine's national army while</b>

347
01:09:57,199 --> 01:09:58,800
<b>Ukraine is defending its territorial</b>

348
01:09:58,800 --> 01:10:00,566
<b>integrity and independence.</b>

349
01:10:00,733 --> 01:10:02,266
<b>So we don't really have to guess why the</b>

350
01:10:02,266 --> 01:10:03,233
<b>Ukrainian state thinks</b>

351
01:10:03,266 --> 01:10:04,699
<b>the UPA name is useful.</b>

352
01:10:05,199 --> 01:10:07,033
<b>There is also a difference between saying</b>

353
01:10:07,033 --> 01:10:08,166
<b>"the UPA fought for a</b>

354
01:10:08,166 --> 01:10:09,433
<b>Ukrainian independence"</b>

355
01:10:09,533 --> 01:10:10,966
<b>and saying "everything</b>

356
01:10:10,966 --> 01:10:12,466
<b>the UPA did was good".</b>

357
01:10:12,933 --> 01:10:14,333
<b>Those are not the same claim.</b>

358
01:10:14,466 --> 01:10:17,500
<b>In April 2022, the rating group asked</b>

359
01:10:17,533 --> 01:10:19,033
<b>whether OUN-UPA should be</b>

360
01:10:19,033 --> 01:10:20,366
<b>recognized as participants</b>

361
01:10:20,366 --> 01:10:21,000
<b>in the struggle for</b>

362
01:10:21,000 --> 01:10:22,366
<b>Ukrainian independence.</b>

363
01:10:22,866 --> 01:10:24,666
<b>81% supported that.</b>

364
01:10:24,866 --> 01:10:26,866
<b>Five months later, the Kiev International</b>

365
01:10:26,866 --> 01:10:28,066
<b>Institute of Sociology</b>

366
01:10:28,333 --> 01:10:29,466
<b>asked people to assess</b>

367
01:10:29,466 --> 01:10:32,033
<b>OUN-UPA's activities during the Second</b>

368
01:10:32,066 --> 01:10:33,533
<b>World War more generally.</b>

369
01:10:34,233 --> 01:10:37,666
<b>43% answered positively, 8% negatively,</b>

370
01:10:37,933 --> 01:10:40,333
<b>and 37% found it difficult to judge.</b>

371
01:10:40,399 --> 01:10:42,199
<b>These are also different questions.</b>

372
01:10:42,633 --> 01:10:45,233
<b>One asks whether OUN-UPA took part in the</b>

373
01:10:45,233 --> 01:10:47,000
<b>struggle for Ukrainian independence.</b>

374
01:10:47,199 --> 01:10:49,333
<b>The other asks people to give an overall</b>

375
01:10:49,333 --> 01:10:50,566
<b>judgment on their activities</b>

376
01:10:50,566 --> 01:10:51,933
<b>during the Second World War.</b>

377
01:10:52,233 --> 01:10:53,066
<b>The distinction between</b>

378
01:10:53,066 --> 01:10:54,533
<b>the questions is important.</b>

379
01:10:54,833 --> 01:10:56,666
<b>Recognizing an independence struggle is</b>

380
01:10:56,666 --> 01:10:57,899
<b>not the same thing as</b>

381
01:10:57,899 --> 01:10:59,433
<b>giving one judgment on everything</b>

382
01:10:59,433 --> 01:11:01,033
<b>the movement did during the war.</b>

383
01:11:01,433 --> 01:11:02,433
<b>This is also where the</b>

384
01:11:02,433 --> 01:11:04,033
<b>Russian argument gets slippery.</b>

385
01:11:04,333 --> 01:11:06,100
<b>OUN-B really did have</b>

386
01:11:06,100 --> 01:11:07,300
<b>an extremist ideology.</b>

387
01:11:07,699 --> 01:11:08,500
<b>It really did</b>

388
01:11:08,500 --> 01:11:10,033
<b>cooperate with Nazi Germany.</b>

389
01:11:10,233 --> 01:11:12,133
<b>And the UPA really was tied to the</b>

390
01:11:12,166 --> 01:11:13,600
<b>anti-Polish campaign in Wolnia.</b>

391
01:11:14,133 --> 01:11:15,166
<b>Those things are real.</b>

392
01:11:15,233 --> 01:11:16,933
<b>What does not follow from that is that</b>

393
01:11:16,933 --> 01:11:19,433
<b>modern Ukraine is therefore a Nazi state,</b>

394
01:11:19,500 --> 01:11:20,233
<b>or that Russia's</b>

395
01:11:20,233 --> 01:11:21,933
<b>invasion becomes justified.</b>

396
01:11:22,433 --> 01:11:24,733
<b>A wartime nationalist movement does not</b>

397
01:11:24,733 --> 01:11:26,533
<b>define an entire modern country.</b>

398
01:11:27,000 --> 01:11:28,699
<b>You do not have to clean up the history</b>

399
01:11:28,699 --> 01:11:30,066
<b>to reject the propaganda.</b>

400
01:11:30,333 --> 01:11:31,333
<b>Poland has its own</b>

401
01:11:31,333 --> 01:11:32,633
<b>version of this problem.</b>

402
01:11:32,866 --> 01:11:35,866
<b>In 2024, one Polish ministry stopped</b>

403
01:11:35,866 --> 01:11:37,533
<b>official commemoration of the</b>

404
01:11:37,566 --> 01:11:38,666
<b>anti-communist fighter</b>

405
01:11:39,000 --> 01:11:41,800
<b>Josef Kourasz, known as Ogien, after</b>

406
01:11:41,800 --> 01:11:42,966
<b>objections concerning</b>

407
01:11:43,000 --> 01:11:44,300
<b>crimes against civilians.</b>

408
01:11:44,866 --> 01:11:46,333
<b>The Polish Institute of National</b>

409
01:11:46,333 --> 01:11:48,666
<b>Remembrance responded that the actions</b>

410
01:11:48,666 --> 01:11:49,966
<b>which deserve criticism</b>

411
01:11:50,233 --> 01:11:51,966
<b>should not erase his contribution to the</b>

412
01:11:51,966 --> 01:11:53,699
<b>struggle for an independent Poland.</b>

413
01:11:53,933 --> 01:11:54,733
<b>I'm not saying these</b>

414
01:11:54,733 --> 01:11:55,833
<b>cases are equivalent.</b>

415
01:11:56,100 --> 01:11:56,866
<b>They're not.</b>

416
01:11:56,933 --> 01:11:58,033
<b>The part I think is</b>

417
01:11:58,033 --> 01:11:59,733
<b>comparable is just a problem.</b>

418
01:12:00,133 --> 01:12:01,966
<b>What do you do with somebody who really</b>

419
01:12:01,966 --> 01:12:03,500
<b>did fight for independence,</b>

420
01:12:03,533 --> 01:12:05,233
<b>but also has serious crimes</b>

421
01:12:05,233 --> 01:12:06,500
<b>attached to the same record?</b>

422
01:12:06,800 --> 01:12:09,033
<b>The UPA and later nationalist underground</b>

423
01:12:09,166 --> 01:12:10,933
<b>really did fight Soviet rule for an</b>

424
01:12:10,933 --> 01:12:12,100
<b>independent Ukraine.</b>

425
01:12:12,500 --> 01:12:14,466
<b>The same movement was also tied to an</b>

426
01:12:14,500 --> 01:12:15,266
<b>organized campaign</b>

427
01:12:15,266 --> 01:12:16,733
<b>against Polish civilians.</b>

428
01:12:16,899 --> 01:12:18,666
<b>The UPA gives Ukraine a historical</b>

429
01:12:18,666 --> 01:12:20,066
<b>example of people resisting</b>

430
01:12:20,066 --> 01:12:22,033
<b>Moscow for an independent state.</b>

431
01:12:22,633 --> 01:12:24,666
<b>And I don't think remembering, or even</b>

432
01:12:24,666 --> 01:12:25,966
<b>admiring that contribution</b>

433
01:12:26,033 --> 01:12:27,466
<b>in itself is the problem.</b>

434
01:12:27,766 --> 01:12:29,633
<b>The problem for me begins if making the</b>

435
01:12:29,633 --> 01:12:31,566
<b>UPA heroic requires cleaning</b>

436
01:12:31,566 --> 01:12:32,833
<b>up the rest of its history.</b>

437
01:12:33,066 --> 01:12:35,233
<b>The extremist ideology, the cooperation</b>

438
01:12:35,233 --> 01:12:36,733
<b>with Nazi Germany and the</b>

439
01:12:36,766 --> 01:12:38,266
<b>anti-Polish campaign in Wolnia.</b>

440
01:12:38,533 --> 01:12:40,966
<b>Those facts belong to the same movement.</b>

441
01:12:41,266 --> 01:12:42,766
<b>Acknowledging them does not mean</b>

442
01:12:42,800 --> 01:12:43,633
<b>accepting Russia's</b>

443
01:12:43,633 --> 01:12:45,366
<b>propaganda about modern Ukraine.</b>

